.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt GZIP 1
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm gzip ,
.Nm gunzip ,
.Nm zcat
.Nd compression and decompression tool using Lempel-Ziv coding (LZ77)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl cdfhklNnqrtVv123456789
.Op Fl S Ar suffix
.Op Ar file ...
.Nm gunzip
.Op Fl cfhklNnqrtVv
.Op Fl S Ar suffix
.Op Ar file ...
.Nm zcat
.Op Fl fhV
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
compresses each
.Ar file
and replaces it with one of the same name and the suffix
.Ql .gz ,
which keeps the original's mode, owner and access and modification times.
With
.Fl d ,
or run as
.Nm gunzip ,
it does the reverse: a file whose name ends in
.Ql .gz ,
.Ql -gz ,
.Ql .z ,
.Ql -z ,
.Ql _z
or the
.Fl S
suffix is replaced by the expanded file without it, and one ending in
.Ql .tgz
or
.Ql .taz
by a file ending in
.Ql .tar .
.Nm zcat
expands each
.Ar file
to the standard output, as
.Nm
.Fl dc
does.
.Pp
A compressed file may hold several gzip members one after another; they expand to the
concatenation of their data.
Data after the last member is ignored with a warning.
.Pp
With no
.Ar file ,
or one of
.Sq Fl ,
the standard input is compressed or expanded to the standard output.
.Nm
will not write compressed data to a terminal, nor read it from one, without
.Fl f .
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width "-S suffix"
.It Fl 1 , Fl 2 , ... , Fl 9 , Fl -fast , Fl -best
The compression level, from the fastest
.Pq Fl 1 , Fl -fast
to the smallest output
.Pq Fl 9 , Fl -best .
The default is 6.
.It Fl c , Fl -stdout , Fl -to-stdout
Write to the standard output and keep the input files.
.It Fl d , Fl -decompress , Fl -uncompress
Expand instead of compress.
.It Fl f , Fl -force
Overwrite existing output files without asking, compress files with other links and
files that already have the suffix, and read or write a terminal.
With
.Fl d
and
.Fl c ,
input that is not in gzip format is copied to the standard output as it is.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Show a summary of the options.
.It Fl k , Fl -keep
Keep the input files.
.It Fl l , Fl -list
For each compressed
.Ar file ,
list its compressed and expanded sizes, the compression ratio and the name it expands to;
with
.Fl v ,
also the method, the CRC and the stored time.
A total line follows when there is more than one.
.It Fl N , Fl -name
When compressing, store the file's name and modification time in the header (the default).
When expanding, name the output after the stored name and give it the stored time.
Only the last component of a stored name is used, and the output is always made in the
directory of the input.
.It Fl n , Fl -no-name
When compressing, store neither the name nor the time.
When expanding, ignore them (the default).
.It Fl q , Fl -quiet
Do not print warnings.
.It Fl r , Fl -recursive
Descend into each
.Ar file
that is a directory, compressing or expanding the regular files in it.
Symbolic links found in a directory are left alone.
.It Fl S Ar suffix , Fl -suffix Ar suffix
Use
.Ar suffix
instead of
.Ql .gz .
.It Fl t , Fl -test
Check the integrity of each compressed
.Ar file
without writing anything.
.It Fl V , Fl -version
Print the version.
.It Fl v , Fl -verbose
Report on each file processed: its name and the compression ratio.
.El
.Pp
Options are also taken from the
.Ev GZIP
environment variable, before those on the command line.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width GZIP
.It Ev GZIP
Default options, separated by blanks.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The
.Nm
utility exits 0 on success,
1 if an error occurred or a file was skipped,
and 2 if trailing data after compressed data was ignored and nothing worse happened.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Compress every file under a directory, at the highest level:
.Dl $ gzip -9r logs
.Pp
Look into a compressed file without expanding it on disk:
.Dl $ zcat notes.gz | more
.Pp
Read files whether or not they are compressed:
.Dl $ zcat -f a.txt b.txt.gz
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr tar 1 ,
.Xr zstd 1
.Rs
.%A P. Deutsch
.%T GZIP file format specification version 4.3
.%O RFC 1952
.Re
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
program was written by Jean-loup Gailly for the GNU project in 1992;
the BSDs replaced it with Matthew R. Green's version, which appeared in
.Nx 2.0
and
.Fx 7.0 .
This one, with its DEFLATE implementation, is written in Rust for OxideBSD.
.Sh CAVEATS
The
.Fl a ,
.Fl L
and
.Fl Z
options of the BSDs' gzip are not provided, nor the expansion of
.Xr compress 1 ,
bzip2, xz and pack data.
